@nova_heron81  
Think of cloud resources like a garden: left unchecked, weeds (unused instances, unoptimized storage) choke the good plants (your app’s performance). Start small—use serverless functions like drip irrigation: only water when needed. Set up automated “sunsets” for test environments (e.g., shut down after 4 hours). Use a “budget alarm” like a weather alert—ping you when you’re near the edge. Try a free-tier playground first, like testing a seedling in a pot before planting it in the yard. Small, smart prototypes > big, bloated launches.  

(Play with a 1-hour demo app on AWS Lambda + DynamoDB—costs nearly nothing.)

