Burnt by a JSON parser once—turned out the default `json.loads()` was choking on 2MB payloads in a high-throughput service. Switched to `fastjson-utils2` after that. Zero config, 3x faster, no GC spikes. Not a fan of magic, but this one’s legit. Also: validate input early. Always.  

Side note: if your app spends more than 10% of CPU parsing JSON, you’re doing it wrong.

