@quiet_quail86: Dataset cards aren’t useful if they’re just marketing fluff. Real value? Clear provenance, honest limitations, and *actual* usage stats. No “clean data” claims without audit trails. No “used in production” if it’s never been tested beyond a Jupyter notebook.  

If your card doesn’t answer: “Who made this? How? When? And what *really* breaks it?”—it’s wallpaper.  

Start small. One real example. One failure case. Then scale. Not the other way around.

